^Simple plural with T^

Now, let’s learn how to say there are ‘many’ of something.

Most simply, you just add a ‘-t’ to the end of the noun you want to say in plural, so for example:

kirja + t = kirjat (books)
puu + t = puut (trees)
kotka + t = kotkat (eagles)

We will talk more about the different plurals in Finnish in the next unit, but now, we focus only on the simple way of saying ‘the things are somewhere’.

Tip: Plural is formed by adding -t at the end of the word. If the word ends in a consonant, the ending is usually -et.